[00:00.00]Let me tell you something that might surprise you.|让我告诉你一件可能会让你意外的事。
[00:02.54]The reason you don't understand English is not because your listening is bad.|你听不懂英语，不是因为你的听力差，
[00:07.12]It's because you're trying to understand too much.|而是因为你想听懂的东西太多了。
[00:10.40]Every word, every sentence, every detail.|每一个词、每一句、每个细节。
[00:14.48]And that is exactly what is slowing you down.|而这正是拖慢你的原因。
[00:17.12]So today, I'll show you the one thing that will dramatically improve your listening skills.|所以今天，我要告诉你一件能大幅提升听力的事。
[00:22.30]And once you understand this, everything becomes easier for you.|一旦你明白了这一点，一切都会变得容易。
[00:26.68]The one thing is stop listening word by word.|这件事就是：别一个词一个词地听。
[00:30.06]Stop trying to understand every word. Start focusing on stressed words, key ideas, the overall meaning in a sentence.|别再试图听懂每个词，开始关注重读词、关键信息和整句的意思。
[00:38.85]And that is how native speakers listen. They don't catch every word.|母语者就是这样听的。他们不会抓住每个词，
[00:43.95]They catch the message.|他们抓的是信息。
[00:45.68]And why this changes everything is because English is not spoken word by word.|为什么这能改变一切？因为英语不是一个词一个词说出来的，
[00:51.02]It is spoken in rhythm.|而是有节奏地说出来的。
[00:52.80]Some words are strong.|有些词是重读的，
[00:54.20]Some words are weak.|有些词是弱读的，
[00:56.08]Some words disappears.|有些词甚至会被吞掉。
[00:57.94]Okay.|好。
[00:58.32]For example, I want to go to the store.|比如「I want to go to the store.」
[01:01.18]Often sounds like I want to go to the store.|听起来常常像「I wanna go to the store.」
[01:03.72]If you try to hear every word clearly, you will get lost.|如果你想听清每个词，就会跟丢。
[01:07.16]But if you focus on stressed words, want, go, stir, you'll understand the meaning instantly.|但如果抓住重读词——want、go、store——你立刻就能明白意思。
[01:16.10]That is the shift from words to meanings.|这就是从「词」到「意思」的转变。
[01:20.10]Focus on the gist.|抓住大意。
[01:21.98]Instead of asking, what does every word mean?|别问「每个词是什么意思」，
[01:25.44]Ask, what is the speaker trying to say?|而要问「说话的人想表达什么」。
[01:28.94]This is called understanding the gist, the main idea, the big picture.|这就叫听懂大意、主旨、整体。
[01:34.24]Even if you don't understand some words, even if you miss some words, okay, you will still understand the meaning.|哪怕有些词没听懂、漏掉了，你还是能明白意思。
[01:40.18]You will still understand what is the speaker trying to say.|你还是能知道说话人想说什么。
[01:43.22]So try to focus on the big picture, on the gist of a sentence, of a conversation instead of every single word.|所以别盯着每个词，去抓整句、整段对话的大意和整体。
[01:49.94]And if you're a beginner and you want to improve your listening skills,|如果你是初学者，想提升听力，
